The $\mathrm{Mo_{X}C o_{X}C}$ confined in uniform carbon polyhedron was synthesized based on trapping of the $\mathrm{PMo}_{12}$ clusters into pre-synthesized, uniform ZIF-67 polyhedrons. The structure of materials can be easily tuned by elaborately regulating the experimental parameters. The catalysts showed excellent performance for water splitting with current density of $10\mathrm{mAcm}^{-2}$ at a low overpotential of $83~\mathrm{mV}$ for HER, and $295~\mathrm{mV}$ for OER. The trapping route not only provide a new avenue toward small-sized $\mathrm{Mo_{X}C o_{X}C}$ , but also extends the kinds of POMs and MOFs those can not be effectively combined by traditional POMOF-based route, and thus expands their application in material fields.
